# =============================================================================
# Git Ignore Rules
# =============================================================================
# WHAT: This file tells Git (our version control system) which files and
#       folders to IGNORE — meaning Git will never track, commit, or push them.
# WHY:  Without this file, Git would try to track everything — including
#       thousands of dependency files, build outputs, and secret credentials.
#       This keeps our repository clean, small, and secure.
# HOW:  Each line is a pattern. Git checks every file against these patterns
#       before adding or tracking it. Lines starting with # are comments.
# =============================================================================

# node_modules/ = The folder where all project dependencies (libraries) are
# installed when you run "npm install". It can contain 100,000+ files and
# is regenerated from package.json/package-lock.json, so there's zero need
# to save it. Every developer runs "npm install" to rebuild it locally.
node_modules/

# dist/ = The folder where compiled/built output goes after running a build.
# For the server: JavaScript files compiled from TypeScript.
# For the client: Optimized production website files (HTML, JS, CSS).
# We don't track this because it can always be regenerated from source code.
dist/

# .env = The environment variables file containing database passwords and
# server configuration. This MUST be ignored because it contains secrets.
# If someone got this file, they could connect to your database.
# The .env.example file (without real secrets) IS tracked as a template.
.env

# *.log = Any file ending in ".log" — these are log files created by Node.js
# or other tools when the app runs. They can grow very large, contain
# sensitive info, and differ per machine. Safe to ignore.
*.log

# .DS_Store = A hidden file that macOS creates in every folder you open.
# It stores your Finder preferences (icon positions, view settings).
# It's Mac-specific junk that doesn't belong in the project repo.
.DS_Store

# test-results/ = Generated test-run summaries (pass/fail counts, timestamp) written by
# scripts/generate-test-summary.js. Regenerated on every run — CI uploads it as a build
# artifact (see .github/workflows/ci.yml) rather than committing it, since it's a
# snapshot of "last CI run," not source code.
test-results/

# playwright-report/ and blob-report/ = HTML/blob output from `npm run test:e2e`.
# Regenerated on every run, not meant to be committed.
playwright-report/
blob-report/
